  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Argolis: above Lerna</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "A mountain peak mentioned by Pausanias whose precise identity and location can not be determined today. Pausanias places it in Argolis, above Lerna and reports that a ruined sanctuary of Athena Saitis was to be found at its summit in his day.",
